  "name": "Surface and recover corrupt event records",
  "slug": "surface-and-recover-corrupt-event",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Make every tolerant event consumer preserve actionable integrity diagnostics instead of silently omitting corrupt audit data.",
    "details_md": "",
    "acceptance": [
      "Flat and sharded corrupt or unreadable event files yield structured EventReadProblem records while valid events remain available.",
      "Per-shard caching never hides an in-place repair of a shard that previously contained a problem.",
      "Index, CLI/reindex/status, storage backend, remote contract, and web API/UI expose event integrity problems with documented warning and exit behavior.",
      "Question and awaiting-input overlays continue to derive correctly from valid events."
    ],
